			<div class="content" id="post-content-4826426">
									

<p>I'm sure others will more ably express my reservations with the story in this article as it is, so I'll confine myself to nitpicking the object class here:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>As the containment of SCP-001 requires an <em>incomplete understanding of its purpose, parameters, and function,</em> the Classification Committee has voted to establish the Atelis object class. Atelis denotes an object that requires the <em>intentional ignorance</em> of related matters, including secondary and tertiary concerns, in order to be contained. Any objects or personnel separated by two degrees or fewer from an Atelis-class object are to be flagged and processed in compliance with established protocols.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>(Emphasis mine.)</p>
<p>These are features that sound, in a vacuum, like a pretty typical Euclid or Keter class infohazard.</p>

