			<div class="content" id="post-content-4826421">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlight:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-#### is a European claymore originated from Scotland. The blade worke the following way:</p>
<ul>
<li>The blade can be used however the wielder wants to use it for (for battle, chopping things, even things you’d normally wouldn’t use a sword for)</li>
<li>Whatever the blade is used for will always be as the iser desires the outcome to be</li>
<li>However after its use something terrible of equal or greater intensity will happen that will affect the user in some way or form.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Along with the sword a journal would be found talking about its creation and its uses, such as a major example the sword being uses by a celt who used the blade to kill an entire army only for a plague to befall his village originating from the corpses that killed the same amount of people the warrior killed. (An additional note, i had a idea for one test proposal being to use the blade to kill SCP-682 but is denied cause if the blade could kill the lizard the concept of what price they’d have to pay in exchange is too grand of a hazard as it could lead to a XK-Class end of the world scenario)</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> the concept of gaining something for a terrible price is a unique concept that has not been explored much in the foundation and i figured it would be interesting especially considering how the saying “Double Edged Sword” is being used literally.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I’m hoping for advice on how to improve the concept and make it more interesting for the reader</p>

